.KEY x
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; xSysInfo's own report, as one more data point (sdcard.md sec.11).
;
; FULL writes to the CLI instead of opening the GUI -- src/main.c's template is
; "DEBUG/S,BRIEF/S,FULL/S,DARK/S" -- which is the only reason this can be run
; from a script at all.
;
; DEBUG: works here, but only because two things were fixed for it: L:debug-
; handler is now built (workbench-fs-debug, which nothing was invoking), and
; make-sdcard.sh inserts boot tests after S:Startup-Sequence mounts
; DEVS:DOSDrivers rather than twenty lines before it. A probe placed before the
; Mount has no DEBUG: device to write to and reports into nothing.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[sysinfo] xSysInfo FULL"
xSysInfo FULL >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[sysinfo] done"
